course: dictionary
lesson: 3161
title: Emoji and meaning in text
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An emoji is a small picture or face you can add to a text message, email or online post. It shows a feeling or idea without words, like a smiling face or a thumbs-up. Emojis are a kind of context too: they give clues about how the writer feels.
explain: The word comes from Japanese. «Emoji» joins «e» (picture) and «moji» (character), so it means a picture character. Early emoji appeared on Japanese phones in the late 1990s.
explain: Clues can mislead, though. Texts have no voice or face, so a joke can look rude. «I'm dead» with the skull emoji 💀 means «this is hilarious», not that someone has died. Read the words and the emoji together, then ask: what does the writer really mean?
explain: Be kind when you choose an emoji. Adding a laughing emoji to a mean post is joining in, not just watching.
fact: An emoji is a small picture used in texts, emails and online posts to show a feeling or idea.
fact: «Emoji» is a Japanese word: «e» means picture and «moji» means character.
fact: Early emoji appeared on Japanese phones in the late 1990s, including a famous set by Shigetaka Kurita in 1999.
fact: In text there is no voice or face, so sarcasm is easily misunderstood; tags like «/s» (sarcastic) and «/j» (joking) can help.
fact: «I'm dead» with the skull emoji 💀 means «this is hilarious» in young people's slang.
exercise: «I'm dead» and the skull emoji 💀 are sent after a funny video. What does the writer mean? | *This is hilarious | Someone has died | The writer is cold | The video was boring
exercise: Which tag in a text warns that a message is sarcastic? | /t | /x | /j | *"/s"
exercise: The Japanese word «emoji» joins «e» and «moji». What does «moji» mean? | face | phone | *character | picture
test: Your friend adds a laughing emoji under a mean post about Sam. What is the kind thing to do? | *Do not join in, and say something kind instead | Like the post so Sam sees it | Add a laughing emoji too
test: Why is a text message easy to misunderstand? | Texts are sent too slowly | Emoji are always rude | *There is no voice or face to show the real meaning
exam: Which sentence best explains what an emoji is? | A Japanese phone with no screen | A long email sent by post | A type of loud music | *A small picture or face used in texts to show a feeling or idea
